As shown in the figure, a rectangle $ABCD$ is divided into nine regions by four lines parallel to its sides, and the regions are colored alternately black and white. Given
$$AP=269,\quad PQ=292,\quad QB=223,\quad AR=387,\quad RS=263,\quad SD=176,$$
find the area colored black minus the area colored white. Here $XY$ denotes the length of segment $XY$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(275);
real[] xx={0,387,650,826},yy={784,515,223,0};
for(int i=0;i<3;++i)for(int j=0;j<3;++j){path p=(xx[i],yy[j])--(xx[i+1],yy[j])--(xx[i+1],yy[j+1])--(xx[i],yy[j+1])--cycle;filldraw(p,(i+j)%2==0?black:white,black+linewidth(0.4));}
label("A",(0,784),(-1,1));label("B",(0,0),(-1,-1));label("C",(826,0),(1,-1));label("D",(826,784),(1,1));
label("P",(0,515),(-1,0));label("Q",(0,223),(-1,0));label("R",(387,784),(0,1));label("S",(650,784),(0,1));
label("269",(-70,649.5));label("292",(-70,369));label("223",(-70,111.5));
label("387",(193.5,875));label("263",(518.5,875));label("176",(738,875));
[/asy]

Three distinct points $D,B,C$ lie on one line in this order, with $DB=BC=2$. A point $A$ satisfies $AB=AC$. There is a circle $\Gamma$ tangent to lines $AC$ and $DC$ at $A$ and $D$, respectively. Let $E$ be the intersection other than $A$ of $\Gamma$ with line $AB$, and let $F$ be the intersection other than $E$ of $\Gamma$ with line $CE$. Find the length of segment $EF$. Here $XY$ denotes the length of segment $XY$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
real cross2(pair u,pair v) {return u.x*v.y-u.y*v.x;}
pair meet(pair p,pair v,pair q,pair w) {return p+cross2(q-p,w)/cross2(v,w)*v;}
size(280);
real c=sqrt(5/3);
pair D=(0,-1),B=(c/2,-1),C=(c,-1);pair A=(2*c/(1+c*c),(c*c-1)/(1+c*c));
pair v=B-A;real t=-2*(A.x*v.x+A.y*v.y)/(abs(v)^2);pair E=A+t*v;
pair w=E-C;real disc=(C.x*w.x+C.y*w.y)^2-(abs(C)^2-1)*abs(w)^2;
real s=(-(C.x*w.x+C.y*w.y)+sqrt(disc))/(abs(w)^2);pair F=C+s*w;
draw(unitcircle);draw(D--C--A--B);draw(C--F);
label("A",A,(1,1));label("B",B,(0,-1));label("C",C,(1,-1));label("D",D,(0,-1));label("E",E,(-1,1));label("F",F,(-1,1));
[/asy]
